ode1 with 7 compressed rotations and copytruncate (so the writing application's open file descriptor stays valid and it continues writing after rotation without needing a signal/restart). Verified via forced rotation with a live writer process: compressed backup created, app.log truncated, and the writer kept appending seamlessly. Completed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol on node1: captured baseline boot_id and healthy state, issued a native reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed the boot_id changed (proving an actual restart), and verified the logrotate config, rotated .gz file, and app.log contents all survived and remain functionally correct post-restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected /var/log/inventory/app.log and confirmed no active systemd service/process owns it (RHEL7, logrotate 3.8.6-19.el7 installed)\",\"Created /etc/logrotate.d/inventory with daily, rotate 7, compress, missingok, notifempty, copytruncate\",\"Validated config syntax via logrotate -d dry-run\",\"Started a background writer process appending to app.log to simulate the application\",\"Forced rotation (logrotate -f) and confirmed app.log.1.gz created, app.log truncated to 0, and the writer process continued appending new lines without interruption or restart\",\"Cleaned up test writer process\",\"Captured baseline boot_id, uptime, and healthy config/log state on node1\",\"Rebooted node1 via `shutdown -r now`, backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed and uptime reset to reboot time, proving an actual OS restart\",\"Verified post-restart that /etc/logrotate.d/inventory, app.log, and app.log.1.gz all persisted, and logrotate dry-run still correctly recognizes and would rotate the target log\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Daily rotation, 7 compressed rotations, config created on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f29f296cfa604c53\",\"cmd-4aa9459bfe91461c\",\"cmd-2b66c170ca1f4505\"],\"summary\":\"Created /etc/logrotate.d/inventory (after resolving permission via sudo) with daily/rotate 7/compress/copytruncate and confirmed file content and permissions\"},{\"requirement\":\"Config is syntactically valid and correctly parsed by logrotate\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5233ddd3bb584789\"],\"summary\":\"logrotate -d dry-run shows 'rotating pattern: /var/log/inventory/app.log after 1 days (7 rotations)' with no errors\"},{\"requirement\":\"Rotation actually works and produces compressed rotated file\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f793c885f34e4300\",\"cmd-3c1ac0f059e544c8\"],\"summary\":\"Started a live writer appending to app.log, forced rotation, observed app.log.1.gz created and app.log truncated to 0 bytes\"},{\"requirement\":\"Application continues writing after rotation (copytruncate semantics)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3c1ac0f059e544c8\"],\"summary\":\"After forced rotation, the still-running writer process (unmodified, unsignaled) continued appending new lines ('app write 7'...'app write 9') to app.log at the same path, and ps confirmed it never restarted\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline healthy state before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-55c36c656d5742ae\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 1a816f1f-858b-4487-af28-54070d4ce684, uptime since 2026-08-26 10:32:51, confirmed logrotate config present and app.log healthy (11 lines)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3e01d69c26d04e18\"],\"summary\":\"Issued `shutdown -r now` backgrounded with nohup; command returned 'reboot command issued' before the node dropped\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node unreachable during restart, then recovered\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c1c5bffa77194bde\",\"cmd-4f8a6b2542ee425a\",\"cmd-ee962d62af5046e0\"],\"summary\":\"Two consecutive probes timed out (node down during reboot), third probe succeeded confirming node1 back online\"},{\"requirement\":\"Proof of changed boot identity (actual restart, not just service bounce)\",\"command_id