p test writer process","Captured baseline boot_id, uptime, and healthy config/log state on node1","Rebooted node1 via `shutdown -r now`, backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again","Confirmed boot_id changed and uptime reset to reboot time, proving an actual OS restart","Verified post-restart that /etc/logrotate.d/inventory, app.log, and app.log.1.gz all persisted, and logrotate dry-run still correctly recognizes and would rotate the target log"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Daily rotation, 7 compressed rotations, config created on node1","command_ids":["cmd-f29f296cfa604c53","cmd-4aa9459bfe91461c","cmd-2b66c170ca1f4505"],"summary":"Created /etc/logrotate.d/inventory (after resolving permission via sudo) with daily/rotate 7/compress/copytruncate and confirmed file content and permissions"},{"requirement":"Config is syntactically valid and correctly parsed by logrotate","command_ids":["cmd-5233ddd3bb584789"],"summary":"logrotate -d dry-run shows 'rotating pattern: /var/log/inventory/app.log after 1 days (7 rotations)' with no errors"},{"requirement":"Rotation actually works and produces compressed rotated file","command_ids":["cmd-f793c885f34e4300","cmd-3c1ac0f059e544c8"],"summary":"Started a live writer appending to app.log, forced rotation, observed app.log.1.gz created and app.log truncated to 0 bytes"},{"requirement":"Application continues writing after rotation (copytruncate semantics)","command_ids":["cmd-3c1ac0f059e544c8"],"summary":"After forced rotation, the still-running writer process (unmodified, unsignaled) continued appending new lines ('app write 7'...'app write 9') to app.log at the same path, and ps confirmed it never restarted"},{"requirement":"Baseline healthy state before restart","command_ids":["cmd-55c36c656d5742ae"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 1a816f1f-858b-4487-af28-54070d4ce684, uptime since 2026-08-26 10:32:51, confirmed logrotate config present and app.log healthy (11 lines)"},{"requiremen